/*!
@defgroup spi
@ingroup mod_communication Serial Peripheral Interface (SPI)
@brief Full-duplex serial communication driver supporting master and slave modes.

@details
The SPI module provides a full-duplex synchronous serial interface for
communication between the MCU and external peripheral devices. It supports
both master and slave operation modes with interrupt-driven and DMA-based
transfer mechanisms.

@section spi_features Key Features
- Full-duplex, synchronous serial communication.
- Master and slave mode operation.
- Interrupt-driven and DMA-based transfer support.
- Blocking, non-blocking, and polling transfer APIs.
- Configurable baud rate with automatic prescaler calculation.
- 4 configurable chip select (PCS) signals with programmable polarity.
- Configurable frame size from 8 to 4096 bits.
- Configurable clock phase and polarity (SPI modes 0–3).
- MSB-first or LSB-first data ordering.
- Continuous PCS assertion for multi-frame transfers.
- RX and TX hardware FIFOs (4 words deep on standard variants).
- Configurable FIFO watermarks.
- Configurable SCK-to-PCS, PCS-to-SCK, and between-transfer delays.
- Single, 2-bit, and 4-bit transfer width support.
- Optional I2S mode on supported devices.
- Asynchronous transfer completion via user callback.

@section spi_modes Supported Modes

| Mode       | Transfer Mechanism | Blocking | API Function                          |
|------------|-------------------|----------|---------------------------------------|
| Master     | Polling           | Yes      | SPI_DRV_MasterTransferPolling()       |
| Master     | Interrupt         | Yes      | SPI_DRV_MasterTransferBlocking()      |
| Master     | Interrupt         | No       | SPI_DRV_MasterTransfer()              |
| Master     | DMA               | No       | SPI_DRV_MasterTransfer()              |
| Slave      | Interrupt         | Yes      | SPI_DRV_SlaveTransferBlocking()       |
| Slave      | Interrupt         | No       | SPI_DRV_SlaveTransfer()               |
| Slave      | DMA               | No       | SPI_DRV_SlaveTransfer()               |

The transfer type (interrupt or DMA) is selected via the `transferType`
field in the master/slave configuration structure.

@section spi_arch Module Architecture

The SPI module is organized in a three-layer architecture:

@verbatim
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Application Code                     │
│          (calls SPI_DRV_Master* / SPI_DRV_Slave*)       │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│    SPI Master Driver           SPI Slave Driver         │
│  (spi_master_driver.h/c)     (spi_slave_driver.h/c)     │
│  ● Instance-based API         ● Instance-based API      │
│  ● Blocking / non-blocking    ● Blocking / non-blocking │
│  ● DMA support                ● DMA support             │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│         SPI Shared Functions (spi_shared_function.h/c)  │
│  ● IRQ dispatching (master/slave)                       │
│  ● TX FIFO fill / RX FIFO read helpers                  │
│  ● Global instance tables                               │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│         SPI HW Access Layer (spi_hw_access.h/c)         │
│  ● Direct register-level access                         │
│  ● Mostly inline functions for performance              │
│  ● Organized by: Module Control, FIFO, Status/IRQ,      │
│    DMA, Clock, Bus Config, TX Command, Data Transfer    │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│               SPI Peripheral Hardware                   │
│      (CTRL, STS, INTE, CLK, TXCFG, DATA, FIFO regs)    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@section spi_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection spi_config_master Master Configuration (spi_master_config_t)

| Field            | Type                   | Description                                                    | Default          |
|------------------|------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|------------------|
| bitsPerSec       | uint32_t               | Desired baud rate in bits per second.                          | 50000            |
| whichPcs         | spi_which_pcs_t        | Chip select signal to use (PCS0–PCS3).                         | SPI_PCS0         |
| pcsPolarity      | spi_signal_polarity_t  | Active-high or active-low PCS polarity.                        | SPI_ACTIVE_LOW   |
| isPcsContinuous  | bool                   | Keep PCS asserted between frames in a transfer.                | false            |
| bitcount         | uint16_t               | Number of bits per frame (8–4096).                             | 8                |
| clkPhase         | spi_clock_phase_t      | Clock phase: capture on 1st or 2nd edge.                       | 1ST_EDGE         |
| clkPolarity      | spi_sck_polarity_t     | Clock polarity: idle-low or idle-high.                         | ACTIVE_HIGH      |
| lsbFirst         | bool                   | Transmit LSB first if true, MSB first if false.                | false            |
| transferType     | spi_transfer_type      | Transfer mechanism: SPI_USING_INTERRUPTS or SPI_USING_DMA.     | INTERRUPTS       |
| rxDMAChannel     | uint8_t                | DMA channel for RX (only when transferType = DMA).             | 0                |
| txDMAChannel     | uint8_t                | DMA channel for TX (only when transferType = DMA).             | 0                |
| callback         | spi_callback_t         | User callback invoked on transfer completion.                  | NULL             |
| callbackParam    | void*                  | User-defined parameter passed to callback.                     | NULL             |
| width            | spi_transfer_width_t   | Transfer width: single, 2-bit, or 4-bit.                       | SINGLE_BIT_XFER  |

@subsection spi_config_slave Slave Configuration (spi_slave_config_t)

| Field            | Type                   | Description                                                    | Default          |
|------------------|------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|------------------|
| pcsPolarity      | spi_signal_polarity_t  | Active-high or active-low PCS polarity.                        | SPI_ACTIVE_LOW   |
| bitcount         | uint16_t               | Number of bits per frame (8–4096).                             | 8                |
| clkPhase         | spi_clock_phase_t      | Clock phase: capture on 1st or 2nd edge.                       | 1ST_EDGE         |
| whichPcs         | spi_which_pcs_t        | Chip select signal to use.                                     | SPI_PCS0         |
| clkPolarity      | spi_sck_polarity_t     | Clock polarity: idle-low or idle-high.                         | ACTIVE_HIGH      |
| lsbFirst         | bool                   | Transmit LSB first if true.                                    | false            |
| transferType     | spi_transfer_type      | Transfer mechanism: SPI_USING_INTERRUPTS or SPI_USING_DMA.     | INTERRUPTS       |
| rxDMAChannel     | uint8_t                | DMA channel for RX (only when transferType = DMA).             | 0                |
| txDMAChannel     | uint8_t                | DMA channel for TX (only when transferType = DMA).             | 0                |
| callback         | spi_callback_t         | User callback invoked on transfer completion.                  | NULL             |
| callbackParam    | void*                  | User-defined parameter passed to callback.                     | NULL             |
| width            | spi_transfer_width_t   | Transfer width: single, 2-bit, or 4-bit.                       | SINGLE_BIT_XFER  |

@subsection spi_config_features Device Feature Macros

| Macro                              | Description                                                      |
|------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
| FEATURE_SPI_HAS_DMA_ENABLE         | Set to 1 if the device supports DMA-based SPI transfers.         |
| FEATURE_SPI_LITE_VERSION           | Defined if the device uses a simplified SPI (no FIFO, no DMA).   |
| FEATURE_SPI_HAS_EXTERNAL_DEVICES_SELECTION | Number of external PCS signals (>4 enables PCS4–PCS7).  |
| FEATURE_SPI_STATE_STRUCTURES_NULL  | Initializer for the state pointer array.                         |
| FEATURE_SPI_CLOCKS_NAMES           | Clock name initializer for all SPI instances.                    |

@section spi_buffer_alignment Buffer Alignment Requirements

Depending on the frame size, transmit and receive buffers must be aligned
as follows:

| Bits/Frame        | Alignment Required |
|-------------------|--------------------|
| ≤ 8               | 1 byte             |
| 9 – 16            | 2 bytes            |
| > 16              | 4 bytes            |

The `transferByteCount` parameter must account for the bytes-per-frame.
Examples:

| Bits/Frame | Number of Frames | Bytes/Frame | transferByteCount |
|:----------:|:----------------:|:-----------:|:-----------------:|
| 8          | 10               | 1           | 10                |
| 10         | 10               | 2           | 20                |
| 24         | 10               | 4           | 40                |
| 32         | 10               | 4           | 40                |
| 40         | 10               | 8           | 80                |
| 64         | 10               | 8           | 80                |

@section spi_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection spi_usage_master_basic Pattern 1: Basic Master Blocking Transfer

Initialize the SPI in master mode, configure timing delays, and perform
a blocking full-duplex transfer with timeout.

@code{.c}
#define SPI_MASTER_INST (0U)
#define TIMEOUT_MS      (100U)

spi_state_t masterState;
spi_master_config_t masterConfig;
uint8_t txBuf[16] = { 0x01, 0x02, 0x03, 0x04 };
uint8_t rxBuf[16];

/* Step 1: Get default configuration */
SPI_DRV_MasterGetDefaultConfig(&masterConfig);
masterConfig.bitsPerSec = 1000000U;   /* 1 MHz */
masterConfig.bitcount   = 8U;

/* Step 2: Initialize master */
SPI_DRV_MasterInit(SPI_MASTER_INST, &masterState, &masterConfig);

/* Step 3: Optionally set timing delays (in baud rate clock cycles) */
SPI_DRV_MasterSetDelay(SPI_MASTER_INST, 10U, 10U, 10U);

/* Step 4: Perform blocking transfer */
status_t status = SPI_DRV_MasterTransferBlocking(
    SPI_MASTER_INST, txBuf, rxBuf, 16U, TIMEOUT_MS);

/* Step 5: De-initialize when done */
SPI_DRV_MasterDeinit(SPI_MASTER_INST);
@endcode

@subsection spi_usage_master_nonblocking Pattern 2: Non-blocking Master Transfer with Callback

Start a non-blocking transfer and handle completion asynchronously
via a user callback.

@code{.c}
#define SPI_MASTER_INST (0U)

volatile bool transferDone = false;

void spiCallback(void *driverState, spi_event_t event, void *userData)
{
    if (event == SPI_EVENT_END_TRANSFER)
    {
        transferDone = true;
    }
}

spi_state_t masterState;
spi_master_config_t masterConfig;
uint8_t txBuf[32];
uint8_t rxBuf[32];

SPI_DRV_MasterGetDefaultConfig(&masterConfig);
masterConfig.bitsPerSec   = 500000U;
masterConfig.callback     = spiCallback;
masterConfig.callbackParam = NULL;

SPI_DRV_MasterInit(SPI_MASTER_INST, &masterState, &masterConfig);

/* Start non-blocking transfer */
SPI_DRV_MasterTransfer(SPI_MASTER_INST, txBuf, rxBuf, 32U);

/* Poll or wait for callback */
while (!transferDone)
{
    /* Application can do other work here */
}

SPI_DRV_MasterDeinit(SPI_MASTER_INST);
@endcode

@subsection spi_usage_slave Pattern 3: Slave Blocking Transfer

Initialize SPI in slave mode and perform a blocking transfer awaiting
master activity.

@code{.c}
#define SPI_SLAVE_INST (1U)
#define TIMEOUT_MS     (500U)

spi_state_t slaveState;
spi_slave_config_t slaveConfig;
uint8_t slaveTx[16] = { 0xAA, 0xBB, 0xCC, 0xDD };
uint8_t slaveRx[16];

SPI_DRV_SlaveGetDefaultConfig(&slaveConfig);
slaveConfig.bitcount = 8U;

SPI_DRV_SlaveInit(SPI_SLAVE_INST, &slaveState, &slaveConfig);

/* Blocking: waits until master drives the transfer or timeout */
status_t status = SPI_DRV_SlaveTransferBlocking(
    SPI_SLAVE_INST, slaveTx, slaveRx, 16U, TIMEOUT_MS);

SPI_DRV_SlaveDeinit(SPI_SLAVE_INST);
@endcode

@subsection spi_usage_dma Pattern 4: DMA-based Master Transfer

Use DMA channels for efficient data transfer, minimizing CPU
involvement.

@code{.c}
#define SPI_MASTER_INST (0U)

spi_state_t masterState;
spi_master_config_t masterConfig;
uint8_t txBuf[256];
uint8_t rxBuf[256];

SPI_DRV_MasterGetDefaultConfig(&masterConfig);
masterConfig.bitsPerSec    = 2000000U;
masterConfig.transferType  = SPI_USING_DMA;
masterConfig.txDMAChannel  = 0U;
masterConfig.rxDMAChannel  = 1U;

SPI_DRV_MasterInit(SPI_MASTER_INST, &masterState, &masterConfig);

/* Non-blocking DMA transfer */
SPI_DRV_MasterTransfer(SPI_MASTER_INST, txBuf, rxBuf, 256U);

/* Wait for transfer completion */
uint32_t bytesRemaining;
while (SPI_DRV_MasterGetTransferStatus(SPI_MASTER_INST, &bytesRemaining)
       == STATUS_BUSY)
{
    /* Application can do other work here */
}

SPI_DRV_MasterDeinit(SPI_MASTER_INST);
@endcode

@section spi_api API Quick Reference

@subsection spi_api_master_init Master Initialization
| Function                          | Description                                        |
|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| SPI_DRV_MasterGetDefaultConfig()  | Fill master config with default values.             |
| SPI_DRV_MasterInit()              | Initialize SPI instance in master mode.             |
| SPI_DRV_MasterDeinit()            | De-initialize SPI master instance.                  |

@subsection spi_api_master_config Master Bus Configuration
| Function                          | Description                                        |
|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| SPI_DRV_MasterConfigureBus()      | Reconfigure bus parameters at runtime.              |
| SPI_DRV_MasterSetDelay()          | Set SCK/PCS timing delays.                          |
| SPI_DRV_SetPcs()                  | Select chip select signal and polarity.             |

@subsection spi_api_master_xfer Master Data Transfer
| Function                          | Description                                        |
|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| SPI_DRV_MasterTransferPolling()   | Polling (busy-wait) full-duplex transfer.           |
| SPI_DRV_MasterTransferBlocking()  | Interrupt-driven blocking full-duplex transfer.     |
| SPI_DRV_MasterTransfer()          | Interrupt/DMA non-blocking full-duplex transfer.    |

@subsection spi_api_master_mgmt Master Transfer Management
| Function                          | Description                                        |
|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| SPI_DRV_MasterGetTransferStatus() | Query status and remaining bytes of active transfer.|
| SPI_DRV_MasterAbortTransfer()     | Abort an in-progress non-blocking transfer.         |

@subsection spi_api_slave_init Slave Initialization
| Function                          | Description                                        |
|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| SPI_DRV_SlaveGetDefaultConfig()   | Fill slave config with default values.              |
| SPI_DRV_SlaveInit()               | Initialize SPI instance in slave mode.              |
| SPI_DRV_SlaveDeinit()             | De-initialize SPI slave instance.                   |

@subsection spi_api_slave_xfer Slave Data Transfer
| Function                          | Description                                        |
|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| SPI_DRV_SlaveTransferBlocking()   | Interrupt-driven blocking transfer.                 |
| SPI_DRV_SlaveTransfer()           | Interrupt/DMA non-blocking transfer.                |

@subsection spi_api_slave_mgmt Slave Transfer Management
| Function                          | Description                                        |
|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| SPI_DRV_SlaveGetTransferStatus()  | Query status and remaining bytes of active transfer.|
| SPI_DRV_SlaveAbortTransfer()      | Abort an in-progress transfer.                      |

@section spi_notes Important Notes

@subsection spi_notes_clock Clock and Interrupt Setup
@warning The SPI peripheral clock must be enabled via the @ref clock_manager
**before** calling SPI_DRV_MasterInit() or SPI_DRV_SlaveInit(). The driver
does not manage clocks internally.

@note The driver enables the SPI module interrupt internally, but interrupt
**priority** must be configured by the application via the NVIC.

@subsection spi_notes_watermark FIFO Watermarks
@note The TX and RX FIFO watermarks are set internally by the driver during
transfer setup. If the application requires custom watermark values, they
should be configured after init but before starting a transfer.

@subsection spi_notes_delays Timing Delays
@note Default delay values (SCK-to-PCS, PCS-to-SCK, between-transfer) are
calculated automatically during SPI_DRV_MasterInit(). Use
SPI_DRV_MasterSetDelay() to override them for slower peripheral devices.

@subsection spi_notes_frame_size Frame Size Limitations
@warning The driver cannot be used with a configuration of bits/frame
greater than 32 bits and MSB endianness. If you need a frame larger than
32 bits with MSB first, the application must handle the data positioning
manually.

@warning If the frame size exceeds 32 bits, the MSB/LSB option applies to
each uint32_t independently, not to the entire frame. The application must
ensure the uint32_t ordering in buffers matches the MSB/LSB configuration.

@subsection spi_notes_slave_dma Slave DMA Restriction
@warning In slave mode with DMA, do **not** initiate a transfer with a NULL
TX buffer and continuous PCS mode. The driver will never complete the
transfer in this configuration.

@subsection spi_notes_reinit Re-Initialization
@note Once initialized, the SPI module cannot be re-initialized for the
same instance until it is de-initialized. Different SPI instances can
operate independently.

@section spi_integration Integration Guide

@subsection spi_integration_files Compilation Units
The following source files must be added to the project build:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/spi/spi_irq.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/spi/spi_master_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/spi/spi_shared_function.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/spi/spi_slave_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/spi/spi_hw_access.c
@endverbatim

@subsection spi_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following directories to the toolchain include path:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/spi
@endverbatim

@subsection spi_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
No special compile-time symbols are required for this module. Device-specific
feature macros (`FEATURE_SPI_*`) are automatically defined in the device
features header.

@subsection spi_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref clock_manager — Required for enabling the SPI peripheral clock.
- @ref osif — Required for semaphore-based blocking transfers.
- @ref interrupt_manager — Required for NVIC interrupt enable/disable.
- @ref dma_driver — Required only when using DMA-based transfers
  (`transferType = SPI_USING_DMA`).

*/